1
00:00:01,879 --> 00:00:04,198
Chapter 84.

2
00:00:04,199 --> 00:00:06,838
Pitch polling.

3
00:00:06,839 --> 00:00:12,914
To make them run easily and swiftly, the axles of carriages are anointed, and for

4
00:00:12,915 --> 00:00:17,558
much the same purpose, some whalers perform an analogous operation upon

5
00:00:17,559 --> 00:00:22,914
their boat. They grease the bottom. Nor is it to be doubted that as such a

6
00:00:22,915 --> 00:00:27,558
procedure can do no harm, it may possibly be of no contemptable

7
00:00:27,559 --> 00:00:32,914
advantage, considering that oil and water are hostile, that oil is a sliding

8
00:00:32,915 --> 00:00:38,594
thing, and that the object in view is to make the boat slide bravely. Quiquang

9
00:00:38,595 --> 00:00:43,479
believed strongly in anointing his boat, and one morning, not long after the

10
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:48,359
German ship Yungfra disappeared, took more than customary pains in that

11
00:00:48,360 --> 00:00:53,479
occupation, crawling under its bottom, where he hung over the side, and rubbing

12
00:00:53,480 --> 00:00:58,115
in the anxiousness as though diligently seeking to ensure a crop of hair from

13
00:00:58,116 --> 00:01:05,399
the craft's bald keel. He seemed to be working in obedience to some particular presentiment,

14
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:11,318
nor did it remain unwarranted by the event. Towards noon, whales were raised,

15
00:01:11,319 --> 00:01:17,878
but so soon as the ship sailed down to them, they turned and fled with swift precipited

16
00:01:17,879 --> 00:01:23,719
flight as of Cleopatra's barges from Actium. Nevertheless, the boats pursued,

17
00:01:23,720 --> 00:01:28,914
and Stubs was foremost. By great exertion, Tash Teego at last succeeded

18
00:01:28,915 --> 00:01:33,878
in planting one iron, but the stricken whale, without at all sounding, still

19
00:01:33,879 --> 00:01:39,159
continued his horizontal flight with added fleetness. Such unintermitted

20
00:01:39,160 --> 00:01:44,435
strainings upon the planted iron must sooner or later inevitably extract it.

21
00:01:44,436 --> 00:01:50,039
It became imperative to lance the flying whale, or be content to lose him. But to

22
00:01:50,040 --> 00:01:54,838
haul the boat up to his flank was impossible. He swam so fast and furious.

23
00:01:54,839 --> 00:01:57,479
what then remained.

24
00:01:57,480 --> 00:02:02,435
Of all the wondrous devices and dexterities, the slights of hand, and

25
00:02:02,436 --> 00:02:07,238
countless subtleties to which the veteran whaleman is so often forced,

26
00:02:07,239 --> 00:02:13,238
none exceed that fine maneuver with the lance, called pitch pulling. Small sword

27
00:02:13,239 --> 00:02:18,999
or broadsword, in all its exercises boasts nothing like it. It is only

28
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:24,679
indispensable with an ineterate running whale. Its grand fact and feature is the

29
00:02:24,680 --> 00:02:29,159
wonderful distance to which the long lance is accurately darted from a

30
00:02:29,160 --> 00:02:34,755
violently rocking jerking boat under extreme headway. Steel and wood

31
00:02:34,756 --> 00:02:40,198
included. The entire spear is some 10 or 12 ft in length. The staff is much

32
00:02:40,199 --> 00:02:46,198
slider than that of the harpoon and also of lighter material, pine. It is

33
00:02:46,199 --> 00:02:51,159
furnished with a small rope called a warp of considerable length by which it

34
00:02:51,160 --> 00:02:55,318
can be hauled back to the hand after darting.

35
00:02:55,319 --> 00:02:59,079
But before going further, it is important to mention here that though

36
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:03,479
the harpoon may be pitch pulled in the same way with the lance, yet it is

37
00:03:03,480 --> 00:03:08,838
seldom done, and when done, it is still less frequently successful on account of

38
00:03:08,839 --> 00:03:13,318
the greater weight and inferior length of the harpoon as compared with the

39
00:03:13,319 --> 00:03:18,359
lance, which in effect become serious drawbacks. As a general thing,

40
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:24,999
therefore, you must first get fast to a whale before any pitch pulling comes into play.

41
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:29,878
Look now at Stub, a man who, from his humorous, deliberate coolness and

42
00:03:29,879 --> 00:03:35,399
equinimity in the dyest emergencies, was specially qualified to excel in pitch

43
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:41,079
pulling. Look at him. He stands upright in the tossed bow of the flying boat,

44
00:03:41,080 --> 00:03:47,719
wrapped in fleecy foam. The towing whale is 40 ft ahead. Handling the long lance

45
00:03:47,720 --> 00:03:52,755
lightly, glancing twice or thrice along its length to see if it be exactly

46
00:03:52,756 --> 00:03:58,274
straight, Stub whistlingly gathers up the coil of the warp in one hand, so as

47
00:03:58,275 --> 00:04:03,399
to secure its free end in his grasp, leaving the rest unobstructed.

48
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:08,359
Then, holding the lance full before his waistband's middle, he levels it at the

49
00:04:08,360 --> 00:04:13,558
whale. When covering him with it, he steadily depresses the butt end in his

50
00:04:13,559 --> 00:04:18,198
hand, thereby elevating the point till the weapon stands fairly balanced upon

51
00:04:18,199 --> 00:04:25,238
his palm 15 ft in the air. He minds you somewhat of a juggler balancing a long

52
00:04:25,239 --> 00:04:30,914
staff on his chin. Next moment, with a rapid, nameless impulse, in a superb,

53
00:04:30,915 --> 00:04:36,359
lofty arch, the bright steel spans the foaming distance and quivers in the life

54
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:42,359
spot of the whale. Instead of sparkling water, he now spouts red blood.

55
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:48,274
That drove the spigot out of him, cried Stub. This July's immortal all fountains

56
00:04:48,275 --> 00:04:54,838
must run wine today. Would now it were old New Orleans whiskey or old Ohio or

57
00:04:54,839 --> 00:05:01,878
unspeakable old man Gahala? Then Tashego lad, I'd have you hold a can to the jet

58
00:05:01,879 --> 00:05:07,558
and we'd drink round of it. Yay! Verily, hearts alive. Weed brew choice punch in

59
00:05:07,559 --> 00:05:14,518
the spread of his spout hole there. From that live punch bowl qua the living stuff

60
00:05:14,519 --> 00:05:17,238
again and again to such gamesome talk.

61
00:05:17,239 --> 00:05:22,274
The dextrous dart is repeated, the spear returning to its master like a greyhound

62
00:05:22,275 --> 00:05:27,238
held in skillful leash. The agonized whale goes into his flurry, the towel

63
00:05:27,239 --> 00:05:32,198
line is slackened, and the pitchpuller dropping a stern folds his hands and

64
00:05:32,199 --> 00:05:36,839
mutely watches the monster die.
